<title>GERMANY: UK's Clarke says G7 meeting was productive.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says G7 meeting was productive.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The G7 meeting of the world's seven top industrialised nations was &quot;productive&quot;, the British Chancellor of the Exchequer, Kenneth Clarke, said on Saturday.</p>
<p>He was speaking to reporters after the Saturday meeting.</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
